# SkyrimTools

The authoritative, complete guide is [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Read it before changing anything here; this file is
the reminder, not the reference.

## Orient

- Nothing to build, no tests. Markdown knowledge in `skills/`, Python/PowerShell scripts in `scripts/`, two MCP
  launchers, an installer (`setup.cmd` / `setup.ps1`).
- Windows-only, Skyrim SE 1.5.97-first. Heavy parts (`houseCARL`, Ghidra, JDK, venv) live outside the repo in
  `%LOCALAPPDATA%\SkyrimTools`, reached through `SKYRIM_TOOLS_REPO`, `SKYRIM_TOOLS_HOME`, `SKYRIM_MO2_DIR`,
  `SKYRIM_GAME_DIR`, `SKYRIM_RE_DIR`. An unset variable means "not installed" — say so instead of guessing a path.
- Check the machine: `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\agents\doctor.ps1` (`-Json`, `-Fix`).
- Skills: `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` + `references/` (index: `skills/README.md`). Read the whole `SKILL.md` and the
  reference it names; corpora `index.jsonl` are grepped for the quoted token to get shard + line.
- MCP: `housecarl` (live load order, records, Papyrus, BSA/NIF, Nexus) and `pyghidra-mcp` (headless Ghidra). Tool names
  are `housecarl_<tool>`. This workspace has `.vscode/mcp.json` for VS Code; other clients: `docs/mcp-clients.md`.

## Non-negotiables

1. New MO2 mod folder for every patch/INI/OAR submod; never write into another author's mod folder; say that it does
   nothing until the user enables it.
2. Merge INIs with `scripts\misc\merge_ini.py`; never overwrite a deployed INI the user tuned in game.
3. No edits to `ModOrganizer.ini` while MO2 runs, and no hand-editing `plugins.txt` / `modlist.txt`.
4. No game assets, mod files or binaries in git.
5. Never launch the game. Finish with "built, NOT tested in game" plus the steps the user must take.
6. Verify addresses/REL::IDs/vtables (`scripts\re\addrlib.py`, Ghidra) before using or quoting them.
7. `.cmd`/`.ps1` are CRLF, everything else LF; keep encodings (FLICK translations: UTF-16LE BOM).
8. Update `AGENTS.md`, `README.md` and `skills/README.md` whenever you add a script or a skill.
